frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-7)^{2}}{{5}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-(-11))^{2}}{{7}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h=-11$ and $k=7.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,-11,7\\,).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264029 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cdab0134-e416-51cf-89fa-73ad4a2c2eb9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Vertical Hyperbola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ec414e7-91e9-5c9e-999f-d7136b85d837" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264031} {:answer/id #uuid "46605ecb-b945-562b-8b82-dba0f42c4a8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298192}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ec414e7-91e9-5c9e-999f-d7136b85d837" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264031} :answer-field/id #uuid "1737981a-75eb-53bc-a464-b390a47d8d81" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264030} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88e0e575-5e1f-5090-9366-b977802a09ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264033}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88e0e575-5e1f-5090-9366-b977802a09ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264033} :answer-field/id #uuid "9081bd80-bc0c-534d-ac33-fac9611c0b94" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264032}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0f2fb430-f525-52b0-8cdc-1b21638d40bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-328296" :question/problem "The center of the hyperbola $\\frac{(y-6)^{2}}{64}-\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{49}=1$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-6)^{2}}{{8}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{{7}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h=3$ and $k=6.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,3,6\\,).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283230 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "223e29c9-1bb5-51ee-9ec8-4d5c15363951" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Horizontal Hyperbola Given an Equation in Expanded Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98792725-41a0-5da0-b5d6-db129288946a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283232} {:answer/id #uuid "85fa5698-91ef-5c47-ba6f-ce806d63abad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98792725-41a0-5da0-b5d6-db129288946a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283232} :answer-field/id #uuid "a46e7f45-4f14-549b-8d34-2661338a50d1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283231} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1591d5c8-2a19-5ea4-9ff8-fe4dff361aaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283235}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1591d5c8-2a19-5ea4-9ff8-fe4dff361aaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283235} :answer-field/id #uuid "3aeef4ab-8348-5c3d-8693-991a60de3e78" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283234}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e9b14a36-f374-5fea-92c5-1f777c17e46a" :question/math-academy-id "q-328355" :question/problem "The center of the hyperbola $4{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-8x+6y=11$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, group the $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-8x+6y & =11 \\\\ 4({x}^{2}-2x)-({y}^{2}-6y) & =11 \\\\ 4[(x-1)^{2}-1]-[(y-3)^{2}-9] & =11 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}-4-(y-3)^{2}+9 & =11 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}-(y-3)^{2} & =11+4-9 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}-(y-3)^{2} & =6 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{3/2}-\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{6} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,1,3\\,).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291471 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "223e29c9-1bb5-51ee-9ec8-4d5c15363951" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Horizontal Hyperbola Given an Equation in Expanded Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72c86939-8c99-5a56-8ffe-383a1b611c26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291473} {:answer/id #uuid "f5884a66-2e21-5b66-bcf5-af8f60d4b733" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291474}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72c86939-8c99-5a56-8ffe-383a1b611c26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291473} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc4a7150-b28b-5f86-bf16-b80258a5f170" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291472} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "baf47612-0907-5263-95fe-e164d900bd4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "baf47612-0907-5263-95fe-e164d900bd4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291476} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fd4b86e-2a1b-5c6a-86a9-1e03505a534b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291475}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "de9dda81-a345-5236-acbb-5d210b78c08c" :question/math-academy-id "q-328358" :question/problem "The center of the hyperbola $4{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-8x+2y=7$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, group the $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-8x+2y & =7 \\\\ 4({x}^{2}-2x)-({y}^{2}-2y) & =7 \\\\ 4[(x-1)^{2}-1]-[(y-1)^{2}-1] & =7 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}-4-(y-1)^{2}+1 & =7 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}-(y-1)^{2} & =7+4-1 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}-(y-1)^{2} & =10 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{5/2}-\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{10} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,1,1\\,).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298193 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "223e29c9-1bb5-51ee-9ec8-4d5c15363951" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Horizontal Hyperbola Given an Equation in Expanded Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9dfbc151-1f2c-54b3-8c71-ec87e9f7d8c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9dfbc151-1f2c-54b3-8c71-ec87e9f7d8c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298195} :answer-field/id #uuid "38fcd900-6613-5154-ba59-51c6f2374047" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298194} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56254e74-9272-5568-982c-bf533c5ddb6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56254e74-9272-5568-982c-bf533c5ddb6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298197} :answer-field/id #uuid "03b5a872-535f-52d9-963a-737701ef0ba6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298196}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8d5e179f-e00d-5e5a-bd63-59577a00dd88" :question/math-academy-id "q-328374" :question/problem "The center of the hyperbola $6{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-24x+10y=7$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, group the $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-24x+10y & =7 \\\\ 6({x}^{2}-4x)-({y}^{2}-10y) & =7 \\\\ 6[(x-2)^{2}-4]-[(y-5)^{2}-25] & =7 \\\\ 6(x-2)^{2}-24-(y-5)^{2}+25 & =7 \\\\ 6(x-2)^{2}-(y-5)^{2} & =7+24-25 \\\\ 6(x-2)^{2}-(y-5)^{2} & =6 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{1}-\\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{6}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,2,5\\,).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298198 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "345d6df7-2ada-5c2e-8146-7c779afae3af" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Vertical Hyperbola Given an Equation in Expanded Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd72eec5-60e3-5ad1-8366-ff64a0970525" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298200} {:answer/id #uuid "5a354e79-e71a-5d26-b5d0-5fe5283c07a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd72eec5-60e3-5ad1-8366-ff64a0970525" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298200} :answer-field/id #uuid "61088245-8d8e-562f-9d95-fa534faab187" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298199} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62f1467a-0158-57f1-ab17-b56d2c1487d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62f1467a-0158-57f1-ab17-b56d2c1487d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298203} :answer-field/id #uuid "38fff906-68f2-57df-a9ea-d14c1f9b382a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298202}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "87d65ea2-9fd9-5985-89f0-95e56e2fd21c" :question/math-academy-id "q-328400" :question/problem "The center of the hyperbola $-16{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-8y+32x=16$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-16{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-8y+32x=16 \\\\ {y}^{2}-8y\\,-\\,16{x}^{2}+32x & =16 \\\\ [{y}^{2}-8y]\\,-\\,16[{x}^{2}-2x] & =16 \\\\ [(y-4)^{2}-16]\\,-\\,16\\,[(x-1)^{2}-1] & =16 \\\\ (y-4)^{2}-16\\,-\\,16(x-1)^{2}+16 & =16 \\\\ (y-4)^{2}-16(x-1)^{2} & =16 \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{1} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{{4}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{{1}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,1,4\\,).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298204 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "345d6df7-2ada-5c2e-8146-7c779afae3af" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Vertical Hyperbola Given an Equation in Expanded Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8c9cce0-f1de-5c33-be26-bda0222ae473" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298206}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8c9cce0-f1de-5c33-be26-bda0222ae473" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298206} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1db9510-4973-57f7-b999-41918a6a3c7c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298205} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ae7a063-b1a6-5511-a145-706bb0801dde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ae7a063-b1a6-5511-a145-706bb0801dde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298208} :answer-field/id #uuid "23500b52-cb2d-547b-b059-e0acbc3c1f13" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298207}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "07a25597-ac78-5d04-91f9-9b08d8dacc3d" :question/math-academy-id "q-328403" :question/problem "The center of the hyperbola $9{y}^{2}-16{x}^{2}-72y=-108$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{y}^{2}-16{x}^{2}-72y & =-108 \\\\ 9{y}^{2}-72y-16{x}^{2} & =-108 \\\\ 9[{y}^{2}-8y]-16[{x}^{2}] & =-108 \\\\ 9[(y-4)^{2}-16]-16{x}^{2} & =-108 \\\\ 9(y-4)^{2}-144-16{x}^{2} & =-108 \\\\ 9(y-4)^{2}-16{x}^{2} & =-108+144 \\\\ 9(y-4)^{2}-16{x}^{2} & =36 \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9/4} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,0,4\\,).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083845 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f99d4fec-bc58-5a09-9fac-38b46f233489" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Horizontal Hyperbola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85ddd94d-90a0-53e3-8abb-b11acbe51e9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7, 6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082437} {:answer/id #uuid "a97c4262-c284-5fde-b161-07cc979c4857" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082438} {:answer/id #uuid "0ca93485-fe8d-5c89-bfc6-22089a5f9947" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082439} {:answer/id #uuid "334e5cc5-b7dc-5a1e-b76b-b82fc9f0449d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4, 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082440} {:answer/id #uuid "66baaf99-5bbe-5603-acdf-75b5b2a2d875" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "334e5cc5-b7dc-5a1e-b76b-b82fc9f0449d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4, 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082440} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb98a281-906c-5c0c-8750-ea5f0e7d4df2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186082436}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ecad8073-32a5-5bcd-a4f6-4e37160bc7af" :question/math-academy-id "q-78254" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{7}-\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{6}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-(-4))^{2}}{7}-\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{6}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, $h=-4$ and $k=2.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(-4,2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264058 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "345d6df7-2ada-5c2e-8146-7c779afae3af" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Vertical Hyperbola Given an Equation in Expanded Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "497cdc95-c50d-5298-baba-6d1ae1802e59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264060} {:answer/id #uuid "0c9aa5c6-04aa-5dc6-a6f3-34b0fd557dc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264061} {:answer/id #uuid "478c00d4-b26e-5865-a66d-153e3da485c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264062} {:answer/id #uuid "46662acd-00cb-5cdc-8797-d45261ea0904" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264063} {:answer/id #uuid "3b179b00-2c55-5cb5-acb2-7fe6996cfe22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "478c00d4-b26e-5865-a66d-153e3da485c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264062} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9e4b4ad-d430-5d15-9844-b414a6cf495a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264059}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0757e929-9428-56e6-9794-2fa909206184" :question/math-academy-id "q-78379" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola \n$-3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+12x-12y=12?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+12x-12y & =12 \\\\ 2{y}^{2}-12y-3{x}^{2}+12x & =12 \\\\ 2[{y}^{2}-6y]-3[{x}^{2}-4x] & =12 \\\\ 2[(y-3)^{2}-9]-3[(x-2)^{2}-4] & =12 \\\\ 2(y-3)^{2}-18-3(x-2)^{2}+12 & =12 \\\\ 2(y-3)^{2}-3(x-2)^{2} & =12+18-12 \\\\ 2(y-3)^{2}-3(x-2)^{2} & =18 \\\\ \\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{6} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center is $(2,3).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264065 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f99d4fec-bc58-5a09-9fac-38b46f233489" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Horizontal Hyperbola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e157b772-ba84-50df-baba-164296320193" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264067} {:answer/id #uuid "1ab443f0-106f-50b8-809a-4a4f0acb65fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264068} {:answer/id #uuid "06ca6a2e-4455-5322-8752-4cfea94c0157" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264069} {:answer/id #uuid "a688d7fa-c6ce-5c93-9778-8e520508e6a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264070} {:answer/id #uuid "23438b5f-9721-5273-94c5-d8a247c141c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264071}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06ca6a2e-4455-5322-8752-4cfea94c0157" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264069} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b9f66f0-12f1-5ace-a8f3-d476e4f05cf1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264066}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "45f8a767-fd63-5ed1-aa77-8691f5b484a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-78860" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{3}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-0)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{3}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, $h=0$ and $k=3.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(0,3).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292905 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cdab0134-e416-51cf-89fa-73ad4a2c2eb9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Vertical Hyperbola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7318ed52-b5d6-52a1-a771-333d18578307" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292907} {:answer/id #uuid "ae6df21f-943c-5bda-a647-56b849766d9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292908} {:answer/id #uuid "3e9e4df3-52af-5a57-9f44-011e417573b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,-7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292909} {:answer/id #uuid "6364d58e-2fd4-5f1f-877f-5b3230936160" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292910} {:answer/id #uuid "82ea2dc5-4aed-5797-8435-8c74b31f1e50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292911}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6364d58e-2fd4-5f1f-877f-5b3230936160" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292910} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f6b5fcd-1080-5de0-9c6e-99bbcb2f126d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292906}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b2096e13-b432-5188-9b2a-286612b8e650" :question/math-academy-id "q-78868" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\frac{(y-7)^{2}}{9}-(x+4)^{2}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-7)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{(x-(-4))^{2}}{1}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h=-4$ and $k=7.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(-4,7).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298209 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cdab0134-e416-51cf-89fa-73ad4a2c2eb9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Vertical Hyperbola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e662f3d9-613c-53c2-96bf-7512b4ff99d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298211} {:answer/id #uuid "cbdabb4a-2026-58d5-8f03-91d5c51b972e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298212} {:answer/id #uuid "71115906-5e08-518e-b0c8-482e0a3f6296" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,-7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298213} {:answer/id #uuid "2125f246-0390-5c87-bf26-797ec154309a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298214} {:answer/id #uuid "dfc86d0a-ea5b-5c0b-8a12-7798bc33c78b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298215}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2125f246-0390-5c87-bf26-797ec154309a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298214} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfea75eb-32ba-5b59-b725-a955553268e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298210}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "90b63b05-2a3f-56b9-841e-2d7ed2d019bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-78869" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{(x+7)^{2}}{6}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-0)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{(x-(-7))^{2}}{6}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h=-7$ and $k=0.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(-7,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298216 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "223e29c9-1bb5-51ee-9ec8-4d5c15363951" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Horizontal Hyperbola Given an Equation in Expanded Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6777155-641a-51e1-8418-666ecdf3b287" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298218} {:answer/id #uuid "12c6c701-45ec-5596-9bd3-e7a267d642bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298219} {:answer/id #uuid "129ba04e-cb08-51f9-acab-686a4ad795af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298220} {:answer/id #uuid "43ce4304-3cf4-5540-852d-10c31efe18b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298221} {:answer/id #uuid "b8617a09-4af5-561c-9def-224b34e33f0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298222}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6777155-641a-51e1-8418-666ecdf3b287" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298218} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3408793-97ac-5b64-92bf-48296a9fb41d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298217}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e5dd8d19-3d8c-50cb-8805-897e6e830e34" :question/math-academy-id "q-78872" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola \n$3{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}-18x+8y=-13?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}-18x+8y & =-13 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-18x-2{y}^{2}+8y & =-13 \\\\ 3[{x}^{2}-6x]-2[{y}^{2}-4y] & =-13 \\\\ 3[(x-3)^{2}-9]-2[(y-2)^{2}-4] & =-13 \\\\ 3(x-3)^{2}-27-2(y-2)^{2}+8 & =-13 \\\\ 3(x-3)^{2}-2(y-2)^{2} & =-13+27-8 \\\\ 3(x-3)^{2}-2(y-2)^{2} & =6 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{3} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the center is $(3,2).$"}]}
